\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ SNB WATCH: Bank Plays A Waiting Game After  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Neil MacLucas  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 739 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 2010\par 13:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 ZURICH (Dow Jones)--The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week to push the franc down from its record high versus the euro spooked the market, giving the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  some breathing room as it tries to counter the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on April 1 has generated newfound respect for the SNB, and the market is now much more wary of buying the franc," said Nick Parsons, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 National Australia Bank Group\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 The Zurich-based SNB declined to comment on whether it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on April 1, when the euro slipped to a record low around 1.4150. The SNB reiterated at its last policy meeting in March that it would act decisively to curb any excessive appreciation of the franc.\par \par \uc2 The euro, which has also weakened against most other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on concerns about Greece's indebtedness, rallied above 1.43 francs after the SNB action last week. It was at 1.4320 by 0900 GMT Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "The SNB had taken a step back from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  since their policy assessment in mid-March, but with the EUR/CHF running the risk of moving closer to the 1.40 mark, it is back in the market," said Reto Huenerwadel, economist at UBS AG.\par \par \uc2 The SNB has cited deflation as the main threat from a strong franc, though data Tuesday showed a quickening of inflation in March. In addition, recent reports have shown rises in the KOF leading indicators and the purchasing managers index, suggesting a robust economic recovery, and spurring demand for the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 "Since the economic situation in \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2  has changed fundamentally since the SNB started to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market [a year ago], \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not as pressing as it once was," said Ursina Kubli, economist at \uc2 Bank Sarasin & Co. Ltd\uc2  in Zurich.\par \par \uc2 Swiss companies have learned to live with a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially versus the euro, though certain sectors do suffer, according to Economiesuisse, the umbrella organization representing local businesses and industry.\par \par \uc2 "While a strong franc is generally unwelcome, some sectors are able to cope better than others," said Rudolf Minsch, chief economist at Economiesuisse.\par \par \uc2 Many Swiss companies have components manufactured in the euro region, and benefit from a strong franc, while others, such as the tourism sector, find it more difficult because all their costs are incurred in Switzerland, Minsch added.\par \par \uc2 "The 5% fall in EUR/CHF this year has obviously worried the SNB, leading it to increase its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to a whopping $116 billion in February, from less than half that amount a year ago," said \uc2 UBS\uc2 's Beat Siegenthaler. Last week's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could have pushed them to $120 billion, he said.\par \par \uc2 The reserves now make up almost half of the SNB's total balance sheet, and represent a significant \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk for the Zurich-based \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Bank Sarasin\uc2 's Kubli said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tool will be used as an "extraordinary measure" only when necessary, she added.\par \par \uc2 Normally the SNB would be expected to raise interest rates in the wake of quickening inflation and signs of economic expansion, but most observers don't expect any tightening until September at the earliest, largely because of the strong franc.\par \par \uc2 "The Swiss economy is recovering more rapidly than its peers, and the franc appreciation has already resulted in a de facto tightening of about 135 basis points this year," said London-based Parsons.\par \par \uc2 This poses a dilemma for the SNB, which would prefer a monetary tightening through higher interest rates rather than through a stronger franc, which could hurt exports, according to Kubli.\par \par \uc2 With exports to the euro region accounting for almost half of Swiss sales abroad, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -driven rise in prices could dull the appeal of Swiss goods at a time when euro-zone demand is already weak, according to Melanie Bowler at \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Economy.com.\par \par \uc2 This may persuade the SNB to scale back, or even abandon, its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy at its monetary policy meeting in June, she said. "By that stage central bankers will have a clear view of whether sustained growth has taken hold," she said.\par \par \uc2 -By Neil MacLucas, Dow Jones Newswires; +41 43 443 8046; neil.macluas@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 08, 2010 07:21 ET (11:21 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020100408e648002pw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
