\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Swiss SNB  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Reserves Rise In Fourth Quarter\b0\par\par\uc2 253 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2010\par 09:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail on reserves, analyst comment.)\par \par \uc2 By Neil MacLucas\par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 ZURICH (Dow Jones)--The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  said Thursday its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose to 94.68 billion Swiss francs ($88.52 billion) at the end of last year, almost double their level at the end of 2008, signaling accelerated buying of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the franc's appreciation.\par \par \uc2 The reserves were also up from the end of the third quarter, when they stood at CHF82.11 billion.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in recent months to weaken the franc against the euro, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its main trade partner.\par \par \uc2 "The SNB reserve data is a clear signal of its determination to check the gains in its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Lutz Karpowitz, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at \uc2 Commerzbank AG\uc2  in Frankfurt.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss government's Chief Economist Aymo Brunetti told Dow Jones Newswires Tuesday the franc's strength remains a risk to economic growth, and SNB's \uc2 Vice President Thomas Jordan\uc2  reiterated in February the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would act to prevent an "excessive" appreciation of the franc.\par \par \uc2 "In buying its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the SNB has also helped fight deflation in Switzerland, by making euro-denominated imports more expensive," said Karpowitz.\par \par \uc2 At 0815 GMT, the franc was quoted at 1.4627 against the euro.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Web site: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://snb.ch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://snb.ch}}}\par \par \uc2 -By Neil MacLucas, Dow Jones Newswires; +41 43 443 8046; neil.maclucas@dowjones.com [ 04-03-10 0846GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100304e634000qq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
