\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Swiss Franc Sinks;  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Spotted Selling\b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Mochizuki   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 684 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2010\par 06:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The Swiss franc fell to multi-month lows against the euro and dollar in Asia Friday as market participants said \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made a rare and aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The euro spiked around 0300 GMT to CHF1.4905, its highest since Dec. 28, from CHF1.4635. The dollar jumped to CHF1.0800, its highest since Aug. 18, from CHF1.0670.\par \par \uc2 Two dealers in the region said they saw franc-selling orders under the name of the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  on the EBS trading platform. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was bidding for euros at CHF1.49, far above the spot rate of CHF1.46, they said.\par \par \uc2 "I've been in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for two decades, but this is my first time to see the SNB doing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asian time," said one dealer.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been talking down the franc, especially since \uc2 Philipp Hildebrand\uc2  became SNB president last month. It \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times last year, typically in the euro/franc cross.\par \par \uc2 Dealers in Asia said there was about $1 billion of franc-selling orders by short-term hedge funds, an unusually big amount, especially for a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  cross that seldom trades actively in Asian hours.\par \par \uc2 Euro/franc is "all over the shop--rumors of official buying interest," said a dealer in Singapore. "It jumped two big figures in a nanosecond."\par \par \uc2 At 0530 GMT, franc was off its lows, with the dollar at CHF1.0752 and the euro at CHF1.4735.\par \par \uc2 The dollar and euro were stronger against the yen as investors squared yen-long positions after steep gains overnight by the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when investors fled risky assets amid stock falls and sovereign-credit worries. At 0530 GMT, the dollar was at Y89.65, down from Y88.94 Thursday in late New York, and the euro was at Y122.90 from Y122.20.\par \par \uc2 But dealers said the bias remains yen-positive as risk appetite is still low due to lingering concerns European public finances.\par \par \uc2 "The European Commission Wednesday approved Greece's plan to reform its fiscal health, but the plan is unrealistic," said Yuji Saito, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade at Calyon in Tokyo. "Along with Portugal, Italy and Spain, they could get a cut in ratings any time."\par \par \uc2 Indeed, the euro briefly fell below $1.3700 for the first time since May 20, showing investors' increasing concerns about the euro-zone periphery.\par \par \uc2 Investors will be closely watching for U.S. nonfarm payrolls data for January due at 1330 GMT. If the report misses economists' forecasts as it did last month, the yen would benefit most, dealers said. Economists in a Dow Jones Newswires poll expect payrolls to be unchanged in January from December.\par \par \uc2 The Dollar Index, which tracks the greenback against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 80.144 from 79.907.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 23:50 EDT / 0450 GMT \par  \par                          Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par Dollar Rates                        2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par  \par  \par USD/JPY Yen              89.65-68   88.99-03   +0.74  89.78   88.90    -3.69 \par EUR/USD Euro             1.3712-14  1.3730-31  -0.13  1.3746  1.3670   -4.22 \par GBP/USD Sterling         1.5735-39  1.5748-54  -0.08  1.5775  1.5729   -2.65 \par USD/CHF Swiss Franc      1.0738-42  1.0663-68  +0.70  1.0794  1.0647   +3.71 \par USD/CAD Canadian Dlr     1.0729-31  1.0740-44  -0.10  1.0744  1.0719   +2.05 \par AUD/USD Australian Dlr   0.8674-75  0.8642-44  +0.37  0.8693  0.8638   -3.44 \par NZD/USD New Zealand Dlr  0.6886-96  0.6862-68  +0.35  0.6903  0.6858   -5.10 \par EUR/JPY Yen              122.96-98  122.19-21  +0.63  123.19  122.03   -7.73 \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Takashi Mochizuki, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2782; takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com [ 05-02-10 0544GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1034 1863 28038 4162   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100205e625000gu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
