\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ FOCUS:SNB May Hang Back On Policy Reversal, Despite Strong Data\b0\par\par\uc2 By Martin Gelnar  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 635 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2010\par 17:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 ZURICH (Dow Jones)--The predicted reversal of the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 's policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may take time, despite signs the Swiss economy could recover faster than originally expected, economists say.\par \par \uc2 Fundamental factors--such as rising demand for Swiss goods and a reduced threat of deflation--suggest an increase in interest rates and an end to extraordinary monetary policy measures could be in the cards this year. In \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's case, these measures mainly consist of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But, some argue, given the paramount importance of the country's export sector, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't rush into abandoning the Swiss franc to the mercy of the financial markets.\par \par \uc2 A premature change in the SNB's policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent excessive Swiss franc strength could choke off the expected economic recovery, \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Economy.com said.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  will end only once the economy shows clear signs of stabilizing and the risk of deflation has subsided further," economist Melanie Bowler at \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Economy.com noted.\par \par \uc2 "Against the backdrop of decreasing deflation risks and the improved export situation, there are few arguments to support the euro versus the Swiss franc," said \uc2 Credit Suisse Group\uc2  economist Fabian Heller. "However, the SNB will aim to continue to reduce volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," he added, pointing at the possibility of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Hopes of a rebound in the Swiss manufacturing sector received a boost from purchasing managers' data Monday, but any recovery will hinge on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's willingness to influence the franc, economists say.\par \par \uc2 The purchasing managers' index posted a 19-month high of 56 points in January, consistent with an economic growth rate of 2% for 2010, economists said. This would mark an impressive rebound from a contraction of around 1.9% last year.\par \par \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  economist Eoin O'Callaghan said the result of the PMI, an important gauge of future economic development, was impressive considering the "very elevated level of the exchange rate."\par \par \uc2 The recent rally in the franc is one of the most pressing economic issues in Switzerland, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  island in the vast euro zone. Given the small size of its domestic market--just 7.5 million residents--the country's economic fortunes hinge on exports. A strong franc puts a strain on exporters, and in times of economic stress, politicians and entrepreneurs are quick to call on the SNB to weaken the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did just that in March 2009 when the global economic crisis was at its worst, effectively making \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  management a mainstay of monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 However, this was clearly a measure for extraordinary times. The SNB cut its key interest rate to a record low 0.25%, thereby depriving itself of the ability to influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with more cuts.\par \par \uc2 The SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on further occasions last year, mostly without confirming it had been active.\par \par \uc2 Under the new leadership of \uc2 Philipp Hildebrand\uc2 , who took charge of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month, the SNB has renewed its pledge to prevent any excessive strengthening of the franc.\par \par \uc2 Traders say the SNB appeared to have sold Swiss francs last week--its first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year. Friday, the euro jumped to CHF1.4770 from CHF1.4635 and the dollar to CHF1.0644 from CHF1.0548, following talk the SNB had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In line with its policy of reticence on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at 1552 GMT, the euro was at CHF1.4727 and the dollar at CHF1.0589.\par \par \uc2 -By Martin Gelnar, Dow Jones Newswires, +41 43 443 8042; martin.gelnar@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 01, 2010 11:06 ET (16:06 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020100201e621003y7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
