\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Swiss PMI Up In January;Fuels Hopes For Quick Pickup\b0\par\par\uc2 523 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2010\par 11:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds background, economist comment.)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Martin Gelnar \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 ZURICH (Dow Jones)--The Swiss purchasing managers' index rose to a 19-month high in January, reviving hopes that the country's economy will quickly recover from last year's recession, figures showed Monday.\par \par \uc2 The indicator, a gauge of economic activity in the next few months, rose to 56.0 points from a downwardly-adjusted reading of 53.7 points in December, beating market expectations of 55.4 points.\par \par \uc2 The series rose above the 50-point level--the threshold that separates economic expansion from contraction--in September, but a slip in December temporarily broke the pattern of improving results.\par \par \uc2 The January advance reflects a rise in industrial output and orders, said \uc2 Credit Suisse Group\uc2 , which calculates the series with the Association of Purchasing and Materials Management.\par \par \uc2 However, the rebound is still fragile. The PMI remains well below levels of more than 60 points registered in periods of rapid economic expansion.\par \par \uc2 Economists said the figure is in line with improving economic prospects in Switzerland and elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 The spike in January shows the economy had a very good start this year, according to ING, with economist Julien Manceaux noting the level is consistent with growth in gross domestic product of 2% for 2010. He also highlighted a better-than-expected upward move in the forward-looking Swiss indicator KOF, released last week.\par \par \uc2 However, much will depend on the confidence of Swiss consumers, which is likely to be shaky as unemployment continues to rise. "For that reason, signs of a strong recovery are still to be taken with a pinch of salt," Manceaux said.\par \par \uc2 BNP Paribas SA\uc2  economist Eoin O'Callaghan said the Swiss PMI data compare favorably with the 52-point reading recorded in the euro zone. "Switzerland continues to outperform the euro area on this measure of manufacturing activity. That continues to impress considering the very elevated level of the exchange rate," he said.\par \par \uc2 The PMI report came after a clear drop in the Swiss franc late last week, sparking speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent a further rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the euro jumped to CHF1.4770 from CHF1.4635 in New York trading hours. The dollar made similar gains, leaping to CHF1.0644 from CHF1.0548.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  renewed its pledge to sell Swiss francs to prevent any excessive appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A fast rise in the Swiss franc against the euro, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the country's most important trading partners, puts a strain on \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's important exporting industry.\par \par \uc2 Last year, the SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times to lower the franc.\par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at 1015 GMT, the euro traded at CHF1.4718 and the dollar at CHF1.0580.\par \par \uc2 The SNB , which has kept interest rates at a record low of 0.25% since March 2009, is expected to maintain that level for some months to come.\par \par \uc2 -By Martin Gelnar, Dow Jones Newswires, +41 43 443 8042; martin.gelnar@dowjones.com [ 01-02-10 1055GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100201e621000xu\par }\page {\par