\par\par \b \uc2 Swiss prices post y/y rise, deflation risks remain\b0\par\par\uc2 287 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2010\par 09:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 * CPI posts first y/y rise in December since February\par \par \uc2 * Annual inflation lower than economists had expected\par \par \uc2 * Core inflation ticks down\par \par \uc2 ZURICH, Jan 7 (Reuters) - Swiss consumer prices rose for the first time year-on-year in ten months in December, data showed on Thursday, but the gain was smaller than economists expected, indicating that the risk of deflation was not fully overcome.\par \par \uc2 The consumer price index rose 0.3 percent from a year ago but was 0.2 percent lower compared with the previous month, the Federal Statistics Office said. Core inflation also declined month-on-month, the data showed.\par \par \uc2 "The index's (month-on-month) fall of 0.2 percent is chiefly due to sales in the clothing sector and lower prices for crude oil," the statistics office said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 For December, economists polled by Reuters had on average expected a yearly inflation rate of 0.5 percent.<ECONCH>\par \par \uc2 To fight the worst recession in decades and combat falling prices, the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  launched unconventional policy tools in March, including ultra-low interest rates, corporate debt purchases and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2  emerged from recession in the third quarter of last year, and the SNB forecasts growth of 0.5 to 1.0 percent for 2010 and inflation of 0.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has begun to unwind some of its unconventional measures, it has also cautioned that the recovery remains fragile.\par \par \uc2 The closely-watched KOF barometer, published on Dec. 30, indicated that the recovery was set to loose momentum this year. [ID:nLDE5BT0UK] (Editing by Andy Bruce)\par \par \uc2 SWISS-ECONOMY/CPI|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100107e617000jk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
