\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ SNB: The Worst Of Financial Crisis Behind Us -Bd Member Jordan\b0\par\par\uc2 516 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 2009\par 19:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2009, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 2 Nov 2009 13:25 EDT *DJ  Time For Exit Strategy Hasn't Yet Come - SNB Jordan\par \par \uc2 2 Nov 2009 13:25 EDT *DJ  SNB: No Credit Crunch In Switzerland - SNB Jordan\par \par \uc2 2 Nov 2009 13:25 EDT *DJ  SNB: Volatility In Swiss Franc Has Decreased - Jordan\par \par \uc2 2 Nov 2009 13:25 EDT *DJ  Dollar To Remain Bellwether \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  For Time Being - Jordan\par \par \uc2 2 Nov 2009 13:26 EDT *DJ  SNB: \uc2 UBS\uc2  On The Path To Recovery - Jordan\par \par \uc2 2 Nov 2009 13:28 EDT *DJ  SNB's Risk Tied To \uc2 UBS\uc2  StabFund At Around $25B - Jordan\par \par \uc2 2 Nov 2009 13:28 EDT *DJ  Long-Term Goal Remains Price Stability - SNB Jordan\par \par \uc2 2 Nov 2009 13:28 EDT *DJ  Monetary Stimulus Must Disappear To Prevent Inflation -Jordan\par \par \uc2 2 Nov 2009 13:28 EDT *DJ  Timing Of Exit Strategy Is Crucial, Biggest Challenge -Jordan\par \par \uc2 2 Nov 2009 13:48 EDT DJ  SNB: Time For Exit Strategy Hasn't Yet Arrived - Jordan\par \par \uc2 BERN (Dow Jones)--The worst of the financial crisis has passed but it would be premature to hike rates, \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  directorate member \uc2 Thomas Jordan\uc2  said Monday.\par \par \uc2 "The worst is behind us but there isn't enough stability to talk about an exit strategy as yet," Jordan said in a speech in Bern.\par \par \uc2 He added the biggest challenge for policymakers is the timing of any exit strategy--the return to a higher interest rate level consistent with long-term price stability.\par \par \uc2 The current stimulus stemming from record-low rates will have to disappear at some stage to prevent a surge in inflation in a few years' time, according to Jordan.\par \par \uc2 However, the path to a normalized monetary policy will be a stony one, he said.\par \par \uc2 "The timing of the exit strategy will be crucial, and it will also be tough to communicate," Jordan said, adding that the SNB's overriding goal remains price stability.\par \par \uc2 Among the positive recent signs are the fact that banks have begun lending to each other and that credit risk premiums haven come down. Also, there is no sight of a credit crunch in \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy begun last March has been successful. "As a consequence, the volatility in the Swiss franc has decreased.\par \par \uc2 He didn't comment on last week's speculation the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to drive the Swiss franc lower.\par \par \uc2 UBS AG (\uc2 UBS\uc2 ), the only Swiss bank that needed government support to survive the crisis, is on the path to recovery, Jordan said.\par \par \uc2 The risk to the SNB stemming from the so-called StabFund, a special vehicle for \uc2 UBS\uc2 's toxic assets, has halved to around $25 billion compared with some $54 billion earlier this year, according to Jordan.\par \par \uc2 Jordan added the dollar will in all probability remain the world's bellwether \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreseeable future.\par \par \uc2 -By Martin Gelnar, Dow Jones Newswires; +41 79 821 5617, martin.gelnar@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 02, 2009 13:48 ET (18:48 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020091102e5b2004sv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
