\par\par \b \uc2 DJ CORRECT:Swiss Ctrl Bk Renews Liquidity Pledge,Rates Near Zero\b0\par\par\uc2 470 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 2009\par 12:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2009, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 ("=Swiss Ctrl Bk Renews Liquidity Pledge, Keeps Rates Near Zero" published at 0908 GMT misstated the expected inflation rate for 2011 in the 10th paragraph. The correct version follows:) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Martin Gelnar \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 BERNE (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday said it is prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to cushion the impact of the economic crisis on the country's economy, and kept interest rates near zero.\par \par \uc2 Switzerland's economic and monetary policy situation is gradually normalizing but risks remain, \uc2 Swiss National Bank president Jean-Pierre Roth\uc2  said at a media conference.\par \par \uc2 "We consider that the time for a correction has not yet come, but that an additional relaxation of monetary conditions is not necessary either," he said.\par \par \uc2 After its quarterly monetary policy assessment, the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  said it continues to target 0.25% in the three-month Swiss franc London interbank offered rate, its rate benchmark. The decision was widely expected by economists, most of whom expect the SNB to maintain the target at the current record-low level for the remainder of this year.\par \par \uc2 The three-month Swiss franc Libor, set each day around noon along with other Libor rates by the British Bankers' Association, was 0.395% Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Renewing its pledge for a generous liquidity supply through unconventional means known as quantitative easing, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would continue to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent an excessive strengthening of the Swiss franc if need be. The SNB started this practice in March, returning to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as an active player after a 15-year absence.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't provide details of past \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but said they were effective partly because market participants didn't know which exchange rate level would trigger an SNB action.\par \par \uc2 According to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders, the SNB has in the past few months bought euros after the euro-Swiss francs exchange rates fell through a psychologically important level of 1.50.\par \par \uc2 SNB directorate member \uc2 Thomas Jordan\uc2  said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also plans to continue liquidity-boosting measures such as the purchase of bonds. Under the SNB's bond repurchasing scheme launched in March, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought Swiss covered bonds for CHF2.5 billion and corporate bonds for CHF300 million.\par \par \uc2 The SNB said it expects the Swiss economy to contract 2.5% to 3% in 2009, unchanged from a previous estimate. Consumer prices are expected to decline 0.5% this year, and to rise 0.4% and 0.3% in 2010 and 2011, respectively.\par \par \uc2 SNB Web site: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.snb.ch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.snb.ch}}}\par \par \uc2 -By Martin Gelnar, Dow Jones Newswires Zurich, +41 43 443 8042; martin.gelnar@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 18, 2009 06:06 ET (10:06 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020090826e56i0nzcu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
