\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ SNB WATCH:Swiss Rates To Remain Near Zero;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 By Martin Gelnar  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 554 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2009\par 15:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2009, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 ZURICH (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is set to keep interest rates near zero and renew its pledge to provide a generous supply of liquidity at next week's policy-setting meeting, economists say.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  was among the first central banks to highlight deflation concerns when it slashed interest rates to a historic low in March, and the economic picture hasn't changed since then. Faced with a worsening recession and a continued fall in consumer prices, the SNB is widely expected to maintain the target for the three-month Swiss franc London interbank offered rate, its benchmark rate, at 0.25% at its upcoming meeting on June 18. Most observers say Swiss rates will likely remain at that level for the remainder of the year.\par \par \uc2 Given the lack of potential surprise over Swiss rates, market watchers will focus more on the SNB's economic and consumer price forecasts next week, and on any comments on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strategy to cope with the economic downturn.\par \par \uc2 "The SNB is expected to continue quantitative easing measures and announce an extension to its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Melanie Bowler, an economist at \uc2 Moody's\uc2  economy.com, said.\par \par \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  economist Marcel Thieliant said the SNB would likely reiterate its stance from March. "We expect the SNB to repeat its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  were meant to prevent an excessive rise in the Swiss franc. We don't think they will say they want to actively weaken the Swiss franc, for instance," Thieliant said.\par \par \uc2 In March, the SNB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in 15 years to cap a rise in the franc after the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained around 10% against the euro between October 2008 and March 2009. The euro subsequently stabilized at around CHF1.51, a relatively favorable level for Swiss exporters.\par \par \uc2 The bank's repertoire of unconventional methods to increase liquidity also includes additional repurchase transactions and the buying of corporate and covered bonds.\par \par \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 's Thieliant said the SNB may provide more details on its bond purchase program next week.\par \par \uc2 The SNB so far hasn't disclosed any details about its bond-buying scheme, unlike other central banks with similar programs such as the U.S. Federal Reserve and the Bank of England.\par \par \uc2 UBS\uc2  economist Reto Huenerwadel said the SNB may be considering broadening the scope of its bond market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , possibly including Swiss government paper.\par \par \uc2 The SNB is also likely to reiterate it's prepared to increase interest rates once economic conditions improve.\par \par \uc2 But that seems a distant possibility with Switzerland's economy expected to contract between 2% and more than 3% this year, economists said.\par \par \uc2 The bank will also provide an inflation update. It said earlier this year it expects Swiss consumer prices to fall by around 0.5% on average in 2009, with a likely inter-year low of 1%. Inflation in Switzerland in 2010 and 2011 is likely to hover around zero, according to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 SNB Web site: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.snb.ch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.snb.ch  }}}\par \par \uc2 -By Martin Gelnar, Dow Jones Newswires Zurich, +41 43 443 8042; martin.gelnar@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 12, 2009 09:34 ET (13:34 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020090826e56c0ncz6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
