\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Japan unlikely to follow SNB in  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 815 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 11:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unlikely, would spark big trade tensions\par \par \uc2 * Broad yen drop also argues against \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 By Masayuki Kitano and Stanley White\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 13 (Reuters) - Based on the Swiss National Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Japan may appear to have reasons to do the same. But analysts say it is unlikely to do so.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the world's second-biggest economy as the world scrambles to combat its deepest financial crisis in decades would cause much greater trade tensions than \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the world's 22nd biggest economy.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this decade Japan spent well over $350 billion to push the yen lower but has resisted the temptation to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far during the crisis.\par \par \uc2 Such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  now would hit a raw nerve, especially as the Group of 20 nations plan in coming weeks to tackle the global crisis that has been compared with the 1930s Great Depression -- a crash made worse at the time by competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluations.\par \par \uc2 "Competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation is not likely in Japan now because the risks of sparking trade friction are too great," said Masahiro Sato, joint general manager of the treasury division at Mizuho Trust & Banking Co.\par \par \uc2 "The Swiss can get away with this because of the relatively small size of their economy and the limited role they play in the global economy," he said.\par \par \uc2 Takahide Nagasaki, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Daiwa Securities SMBC, agreed:\par \par \uc2 "A simple comparison between the two countries cannot be made, and it is difficult to say that SNB's move will open the door for Japan to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said\par \par \uc2 The SNB announced bold steps on Thursday to fight deflation and underpin the economy. It cut interest rates virtually to zero, reflecting moves by the United States, Japan and Britain, but stunned markets by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the Swiss franc.\par \par \uc2 That made the SNB the first major \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets during the crisis, raising the prospect its actions could spark a round of competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluations as governments move to protect their economies.\par \par \uc2 In response to the SNB's actions, the euro posted its biggest one-day gain against the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and heads turned towards Japan.\par \par \uc2 LEGACY\par \par \uc2 Switzerland and Japan face similar economic difficulties that a weaker domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  might help offset.\par \par \uc2 Like Switzerland, Japan is facing the threat of deflation. Both countries are seeing exports demand shrink as world trade crumbles. In both cases, their export efforts are being hampered by relatively strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Indeed, Japan's exports are falling at a record pace and the economy is already in its deepest recession since 1974.\par \par \uc2 But most importantly, Japan spent 35 trillion yen ($358 billion) in the 15 months to March 2004 to prevent a strong yen from snuffing out an economic recovery and worsening deflation.\par \par \uc2 The historical precedent makes Japan the most obvious candidate to follow the SNB, strategists at UBS said in a client note.\par \par \uc2 But despite that legacy, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which decides on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has resisted the urge to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far during the crisis, despite strong temptations.\par \par \uc2 It declined to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in October when the Group of Seven industrial powers issued a rare inter-meeting statement singling out yen volatility, giving Japanese authorities the green light to stem its surge.\par \par \uc2 Even when the yen hit a 13 1/2-year high of 87.10 per dollar in January and exports demand collapsed, the BOJ held back.\par \par \uc2 Now, the yen has fallen back and stood near 97.95 yen on Friday, putting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  further in doubt, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 DIPLOMACY\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's surprise move came just before the financial heads from the Group of 20 countries meet in England to prepare for a G20 summit in April. Avoiding trade protectionism is a main part of the agenda.\par \par \uc2 "Japan would not want to weaken the yen when the G20 countries are trying to hold protectionism at bay," Nagasaki said.\par \par \uc2 A significant factor behind Japan's heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2003 and 2004 was the state of the global economy.\par \par \uc2 At that time Japan was facing difficulties when other economies were in a much healthier state, said Toru Umemoto, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for Japan at Barclays Capital.\par \par \uc2 "Currently, almost all countries are suffering from the financial crisis and the global recession ... If Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market currently it would be severely criticised," Umemoto said.\par \par \uc2 That seems especially true given Japan's large presence in the global economy and role as a major exporter.\par \par \uc2 "A weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not necessarily a cure-all because it can fuel capital flight. Japan certainly doesn't want to take on that risk," Mizuho's Sato said. ($1=97.66 Yen) (Additional reporting by Charlotte Cooper and Shinichi Saoshiro; Editing by Neil Fullick)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /YEN (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090313e53d000qy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw181\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2715\pichgoal600
