\par\par \b \uc2 SNB may  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in markets to help economy-Jordan\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sven Egenter   \par \uc2 580 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Januar 2009\par 17:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WEINFELDEN, \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jan 15 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  will use means like market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  if needed to help the economy weather the unavoidable recession as interest rates are practically at zero, SNB board member Thomas Jordan said on Thursday. The once-in-a-lifetime financial market crisis has triggered a massive global recession, hitting Switzerland's main growth driver exports, Jordan said in the text of a speech to be held at a business event in the Swiss town Weinfelden.\par \par \uc2 "Despite all uncertainties, it seems almost unavoidable from today's point of view that the Swiss economy will fall into a recession in 2009," Jordan said, repeating the SNB's December forecast of a 0.5 to 1.0 percent drop in gross domestic product.\par \par \uc2 (For abstracts of Jordan's speech click on [ID:nLF539965])\par \par \uc2 The SNB already reacted with four cuts of its target for the 3-month Swiss franc LIBOR by a total of 2.25 percentage points to just 0.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 "With the current de-facto zero-interest-rate policy the arsenal of monetary policy options has not been used up by any means," Jordan said. "The expansionary degree of monetary policy can be increased through a number of alternative instruments if necessary.\par \par \uc2 "Market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  beyond the money market or the extension of the duration of our money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  are for example conceivable," he said.\par \par \uc2 INFLATION\par \par \uc2 Jordan said the inflation outlook had improved significantly recently due to the fall in oil prices.\par \par \uc2 "All in all, the Swiss economy faces an extremely difficult year," he said. "Downward risks dominate as regards growth, while inflation risks tend to be balanced."\par \par \uc2 The SNB has already added a number of new tools such as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps to its monetary policy kit to bring the three-month LIBOR down.\par \par \uc2 The rates in its Swiss franc funding offers are at 0.05 percent now and economists expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to use unorthodox measures to ease conditions with many betting on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the Swiss franc.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been rising again in recent days against the euro, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Switzerland's main export markets, making Swiss products more expensive abroad and dealing exporters an additional blow, Jordan noted.\par \par \uc2 BANK LENDING\par \par \uc2 Jordan said that the Swiss economy was well placed to weather the crisis after the five-year boom as the government's and companies' finances were sound and the banking system fundamentally healthy.\par \par \uc2 In October, Switzerland had to bail out its largest bank \uc2 UBS\uc2  after some $50 billion in writedowns related to the crisis triggered by the collapse of the U.S. housing market.\par \par \uc2 Jordan said it was crucial banks resumed lending to each other and that the SNB would foster efforts to get excess liquidity from the state-controlled and regional banks to the big banks.\par \par \uc2 While the SNB had no indications for a credit crunch so far, risks remained, Jordan said. "The economic slowdown might still trigger a tightening of credit conditions," he said.\par \par \uc2 The slump in exports had already started an economic domino effect, Jordan said. The manufacturers were cutting production and investments and were to lay off workers. Consumers' mood had turned gloomy already and they would cut spending eventually.\par \par \uc2 For a factbox on the SNB's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  options click on [ID:nLE386615] (Editing by Andy Bruce)\par \par \uc2 SWISS-SNB/JORDAN (URGENT)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020090115e51f001lo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
