\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Swiss cenbank says would  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  if franc jumps. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Karen Iley \par \uc2 553 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2003\par 12:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  FRIBOURG, \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 , June 26 (Reuters) - The Swiss National Bank would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if the Swiss franc spikes higher and threatens to hamper a recovery in the Swiss economy, SNB Chairman Jean-Pierre Roth said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Speaking to Swiss watchmakers, who have been hit hard by recent franc strength which makes their goods dearer abroad, Roth reiterated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  considered its current expansive monetary policy stance appropriate as long as inflation was low. \par \par \uc2  "Deflation associated with a significant and lasting contraction in demand and production seems unlikely, as long as the Swiss franc does not rise strongly," he said in the text of a speech to the Swiss Federation of Watchmakers' annual meeting. \par \par \uc2  "In this case, we would take the necessary measures to reestablish the appropriate monetary conditions, including directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," he added. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said that with interest rates already near zero, they would be ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to quell any sharp rise in the Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2  When asked if he stood by those comments, Roth told reporters: "Indeed we are sticking to our policy. It is appropriate to our present situation." \par \par \uc2  Roth said Wednesday's 25 basis point cut in U.S. interest rates was good news. "Any effort made to strengthen the (United States) economy is good news for us," he said, but reiterated that the SNB saw zero growth in the Swiss economy in 2003. \par \par \uc2  While Roth signalled that the SNB was satisfied with the development of the franc against the euro, the weakness of the dollar was still a concern as a potential threat to any upturn in the battered Swiss economy. \par \par \uc2  "We are pleased to see the franc has weakened vis-a-vis the euro," Roth told reporters, but added in his speech: "The fall in the rate of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  penalises firms which export to the dollar zone, particularly watch exports." \par \par \uc2  "The National Bank is well aware of the problems which the recent correction in the dollar poses for our economy." \par \par \uc2  Exports account for some 45 percent of Swiss gross domestic product and Switzerland is home to big export players such as the world's biggest watchmaker Swatch. \par \par \uc2  Data released on Thursday showed that while overall exports rose slightly in May as the Swiss franc eased, sales of luxury goods such as timepieces continued to fall and imports to the stagnating domestic economy dipped further. \par \par \uc2  "The watch business is suffering from the value of the franc against the U.S. dollar because we export a lot of products to the dollar zone," Jean-Daniel Pasche, president of the Federation, told journalists ahead of the annual meeting. \par \par \uc2  Pasche acknowledged that the SNB's hands were tied by near-zero interest rates, but warned that the watch industry faced a tough year after a six percent decline in sales in the first five months. \par \par \uc2  The SNB has reiterated that cutting rates to the current target band of 0.0-0.75 percent had created the right conditions for Switzerland to benefit from an upturn in the global economy. \par \par \uc2  "Monetary policy (in Switzerland) is currently expansive and it will remain so as long as price stability is not threatened," Roth said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030626dz6q00j5m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
