\par\par \b \uc2  SNB Rules Out Major  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  To Weaken Franc/Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2003\par 11:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  FRIBOURG, \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2  -(Dow Jones)- Swiss National Bank President Jean-Pierre Roth Thursday said he doesn't expect the economy to grow in the second quarter of this year and ruled out substantial \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the Swiss franc against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "We knew that the dollar was overvalued when it was worth CHF1.80, it is certainly today nearer to a balanced exchange rate," Roth said in a speech to the Federation of the Swiss watch industry. \par \par \uc2  Roth ruled out any substantial \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the Swiss franc against the dollar, as some exporters are asking. \par \par \uc2  However, Roth reiterated the SNB would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the Swiss franc weakened too much against the euro, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Switzerland's main trading partners. \par \par \uc2  At 0916 GMT, the euro was trading at CHF1.5406, well above what is seen as the exporters' pain threshold at CHF1.52. The U.S. dollar was trading at CHF1.3424. \par \par \uc2  Roth said the SNB's expansive monetary policy is adequate for the current weak economic conditions and prevents the Swiss franc strengthening against the euro. \par \par \uc2  In the last two years the SNB has cut key interest rates by 3.25 percentage points. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's range for three-month Libor is 0.0%-0.75%, targeting 0.25%. \par \par \uc2  Roth said that before the Swiss economy starts to grow again exports have to increase, but that needed a global economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  Roth said that he considered deflation to be a minimal risk as long as the Swiss franc didn't appreciate considerably. However, Roth said consumer prices may fall in some months due to lower prices for imported goods. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  predicts an average inflation rate of 0.6% for this year, slowing to 0.4% next year and then rising to 1.2% in 2005. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Web Site: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.snb.ch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.snb.ch}}}\par \par \uc2  -By Antonio Ligi, Dow Jones Newswires; +41 1 212 21 81; antonio.ligidowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030626dz6q000kr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
