\par\par \b \uc2  Swiss money mkt sees rate cut over franc strength. \b0\par\par\uc2 671 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2003\par 11:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ZURICH, Feb 26 (Reuters) - Swiss money market is increasingly speculating on an imminent interest rate cut by the Swiss National Bank, with the talk fanned by SNB comments that it was concerned over the strength of the Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  added fuel to the fire, they said, by providing ample money market liquidity on Wednesday, bidding to nudge market rates down so that it could also cite falling market rates as additional justification for a rate cut. \par \par \uc2  "If you look at the curve, then you can see that (the market) is expecting a cut," one dealer at a Swiss bank said. \par \par \uc2  Money market futures have been gaining in recent days, with June contracts  pointing to three-month market rates of 0.45 percent by the summer. That is a solid 30 basis points below the SNB's target rate. \par \par \uc2  The SNB offered overnight and two-week liquidity via repurchase agreements. It left the repo rate at 0.50 percent for now , below overnight and tomorrow/next rates in the market at 0.60 to 0.70 percent. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With the franc trading below 1.36 to the dollar  and around 1.46 to the\par euro          , the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it was keeping a wary eye on\par developments.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We are concerned about the rise in the Swiss franc, which is under the\par current economic circumstances especially unwelcome," SNB spokesman\par Werner Abegg told Reuters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He declined to comment on what the particular pain threshold for the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might be and would not be drawn on how the SNB might react to\par the latest rise in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We never talk about levels, it is the dynamics which are of concern,"\par Abegg said. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has said it aims to slow any rapid and\par dramatic rise rather than stop it outright.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par FRANC STRENGTH BLOCKS ECONOMIC RECOVERY\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The franc's rise on the euro - the unit of Switzerland's main trading\par partner, Germany - is making life hard for Swiss exporters already\par suffering from weak domestic demand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market players see further room for a cut in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Switzerland\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's already low\par rates or \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb the franc, which could give\par the economy a much-needed boost.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "To weaken the franc, they (SNB) won't do that first with a rate cut,\par but rather \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market," the dealer said.\par "A rate cut will be the very last resort becuase they hardly have any\par powder left."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Should the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reduce rates, the SNB would only make\par a move if the franc spiked higher versus the euro.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The SNB now targets the middle of a 0.25-1.25 percent range for the\par three-month London Interbank Offered Rate - its benchmark - but the\par repo rate already undercuts that midpoint.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Libor was fixed at 0.57667 percent  on Tuesday, also below the midpoint\par of the target range of 0.75 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers say the SNB is likely to nudge down that goal to the repo rate\par level. Alternatively, it might lower the repo rate and shift the target\par to the lower end of the range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par WEAK DATA UPS PRESSURE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Earlier this week, Switzerland recorded its biggest trade deficit in 20\par months as the flat global economy and strong franc strangled exports,\par while figures showed that employment also fell in the last quarter of\par 2002.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts will closely watch fourth-quarter GDP figures which are\par expected to show growth of only between 0.4 to 0.7 percent\par year-on-year, compared to 0.6 percent for the third quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The numbers are due out on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par An upturn in the Swiss economy is not expected before the second half\par of 2003, especially if a war in Iraq further dents the global economy\par through rising oil prices.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar was at 1.3573/78 francs after changing hands at 1.3546/51\par francs late on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro was at 1.4606/11 francs, practically unchanged from the rate\par late on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030226dz2q00kuj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
