\par\par \b \uc2  Swiss franc firms on dollar ahead of U.N. report. \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2003\par 09:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ZURICH, Jan 27 (Reuters) - The Swiss franc firmed further on the dollar in early European trade on Monday, touching levels not seen in just over four years, with players cautious on the outlook for the greenback ahead of a U.N. report on Iraq. \par \par \uc2  The dollar  eased to 1.3535/41 francs from 1.3565/70 late on Friday, hitting levels not seen since December 1998 as U.S. rhetoric on Iraqi disarmament war remained tough, even in the face of dissent of by Western partners. \par \par \uc2  The euro  eased slightly to 1.4661/63 francs from 1.4665/75. \par \par \uc2  U.N. arms inspectors, presenting a key report to the Security Council later on Monday, are expected to say Iraq has not been fully cooperative and that inspections need more time to be conclusive. \par \par \uc2  In the absence of a "smoking gun", London and Washington may have a tough job persuading Council members and Western partners that war on Iraq is justified. The U.S. meanwhile insists there is evidence that Iraq has weapons of mass destruction. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that with such geopoltical issues unresolved, there was scope for further franc strengthening. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, they did not expect the Swiss National Bank to do more to brake the franc than talking it down. \par \par \uc2  Outgoing SNB Vice President Bruno Gehrig said on Friday \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was definitely an instrument of monetary policy in \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "But I'm not saying we will do it tomorrow," he added. \par \par \uc2  The SNB has to date been coy on what franc level would trigger action, leaving dealers with the impression that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is basically powerless against the franc's rise. \par \par \uc2  While Gehrig's comments reinforce the SNB's stated intention to act, analysts say words from a departing directorate member were less likely to change the course of trading in a major way. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030127dz1r00g7h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
