\par\par \b \uc2  Swiss  \highlight22\uc2 fx intervention \highlight\uc2  seen likely as tension rises. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 736 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2002\par 15:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Oct 4 (Reuters) - The threat of a U.S.-led war against Iraq is drawing money to the safety of the Swiss franc, increasing the likelihood the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rein in its runaway \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Switzerland's political and military neutrality and its large current account surplus make it an attractive place to put money at times of war. \par \par \uc2  But the country's own domestic picture is one of a stagnating economy, which needs a weaker franc in order to find buyers for its exports. \par \par \uc2  "Switzerland has been the slowest growing economy in the OECD since 1990, even slower than Japan - the motivation is not really economic for money going in there," said Steven Englander, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Citibank. \par \par \uc2  "The Swiss authorites would prefer to see the world return to a less risk-averse stance - they are going to talk a lot about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  being too strong, and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is definitely a possibility." \par \par \uc2  The Swiss franc has closely followed the tensions between the United States and Iraq. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened sharply last month when Iraq first agreed to let weapons inspectors into the country under existing U.N. conditions, easing fears of war. \par \par \uc2  But the franc strengthened as the United States made it clear it sought a new tougher U.N. resolution. \par \par \uc2  Credit Suisse First Boston said on Friday it revised its three-month forecast for the euro/Swiss franc rate down to 1.46 francs from 1.48 . \par \par \uc2  "War risk is limiting imminent Swiss franc weakness, despite weak fundamentals," analysts at CSFB said in a client note. \par \par \uc2  ECONOMICS - WHO CARES? \par \par \uc2  Data on Friday showed the number of Swiss jobless topped the psychologically key 100,000 level in September for the first time since April 1999. \par \par \uc2  This followed the release this week of the Swiss purchasing managers' index for September, which indicated a further contraction in Swiss manufacturing. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said poor domestic Swiss data was not playing a key part in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading decisions. \par \par \uc2  "Traders don't look at the Swiss data, they don't really care about Switzerland," said Jan Poser, analyst at Sarasin in Zurich. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss National Bank is aware of the problem. \par \par \uc2  SNB vice chairman Bruno Gehrig last week issued a rare warning of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the franc if a sharp rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  threatened to hurt the economy. \par \par \uc2  "This is a measure of last resort, we have never used it in the recent past," he said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to cut rates or even \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the franc returns to a record high around 1.44 per euro hit last September and approached once more in July. \par \par \uc2  The value of the franc against the euro is of the most concern, because the euro zone is \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main trading partner. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not in the SNB's tradition but I would not exclude it," said Poser. \par \par \uc2  "Every time we reach levels around 1.44 we see some sort of action - rumours about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or rate cuts on two occasions." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2  last cut rates at the end of July, dropping its benchmark target range for three-month London Interbank Offered Rate (LIBOR) to 0.25-1.25 percent. The SNB effectively targets the middle of that range, or 0.75 percent. \par \par \uc2  RACING AHEAD \par \par \uc2  Phil Roberts, technical analyst at Barclays Capital, said the charts pointed to a strong upmove for the franc, and he said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could revisit 1.44 by the end of the month. \par \par \uc2  The franc strengthened to a two-month high of 1.4540 per euro earlier this week. It is currently holding a little above a key chart level at 1.4640, Roberts said. \par \par \uc2  "The Swiss franc has been locked in a clearly defined appreciation trend against the euro, or the deutschemark, ever since 1993." \par \par \uc2  The worsening global growth outlook is also dulling investors' appetites for riskier markets, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "Weak stock markets, weak growth, and all this talk of war - this is exactly the environment where a safe haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is well bid," said Michael Klawitter, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at WestLB. \par \par \uc2  But analysts remained doubtful that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could work, particularly when undertaken in isolation by a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rather than as a concerted action. \par \par \uc2  "They could try \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it's not clear whether it would be successful," said Englander. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021004dya400q38\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
