\par\par \b \uc2  DAVOS-Mundell urges ECB  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  to aid euro. \b0\par\par\uc2 339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2000\par 17:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  DAVOS, \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jan 28 (Reuters) - Nobel price-winning economist Robert Mundell on Friday urged the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stop the euro's slide. \par \par \uc2  "I think it's a good time for the ECB to act. The ECB should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market both spot and forward," Mundell said on the fringes of the World Economic Forum's annual meeting here. \par \par \uc2  On Friday afternoon the euro EUR=) fell to a record low against the dollar, piercing key support at 97.79 cents and trading down to 97.39 cents. \par \par \uc2  Mundell said the ECB could even act on its own without consulting the Federal Reserve or the Bank of Japan. However, in the long run these countries have to agree, he stressed. \par \par \uc2  He said that despite the euro's continuous slide over the past year, the single European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was credible. \par \par \uc2  "The euro has been credible so far," he said. This was reflected in higher forward than spot rates of the euro throughout 1999, he said, explaining this reflected the market's expectation of a higher rate in the future. \par \par \uc2  A factor that should push the euro higher was the increasing demand of central banks for the euro as a reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "By 2010 central banks would want to hold the same amounts of euros and dollars in reserves," he said. \par \par \uc2  The ECB should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  because a further decline of the euro exchange rate would result in higher import prices and consequently increased wage demands, pushing inflation in the euro zone up. \par \par \uc2  "That would force a tighter monetary policy," he said. \par \par \uc2  He said the ECB should not ignore the euro. "If the ECB neglects the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate it would neglect one of the most important early indicators of inflation." \par \par \uc2  Turning to the overall volatility between the euro and dollar, Mundell said: "I don't believe the dollar euro rate would fluctuate like the mark/dollar rate did in the past." \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw1s05188\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
