\par\par \b \uc2  SNB's Roth sees stable euro/Swiss franc rate. \b0\par\par\uc2 561 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 1998\par 10:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ZURICH, Nov 23 (Reuters) - Swiss National Bank Vice-Chairman Jean-Pierre Roth said the Swiss franc would probably be stable against the euro as financial markets came to realise that the two were really "sister \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ". \par \par \uc2  In the text of a speech to be delivered at a financial seminar in Vienna, Roth said the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's priority to maintain price stability dovetailed perfectly with the SNB's monetary stance. \par \par \uc2  Also, experience has shown that converging fundamentals and similar policy objectives provide a good chance that exchange rates between the euro and the franc will remain within an acceptable fluctuation band, he said without elaborating. \par \par \uc2  He noted that the franc had firmed against the mark at a low annual rate of 0.5 percent from 1983 to 1998 and had fluctuated within a band of plus or minus five percent even without the SNB's having \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  "The more \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2  behaves like a European country, the greater the chance of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability between the Swiss franc and the euro," he said. \par \par \uc2  "We are thus confident that that the absence of major tensions observable over the last two years will be an enduring phenomenon and that the market will gradually come to recognise that the Swiss franc and the euro are two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  belonging to the same European family." \par \par \uc2  He said the euro would probably be used frequently by Swiss companies, which would make the franc less widely used to pay for foreign trade transactions. Travellers will also find it easier to use euros. \par \par \uc2  "Given the very close relations between Switzerland and Euroland, the exchange rate sensitivity of the Swiss economy is expected to increase, which will require not only an efficient clearing system but also tight management of exchange rate risks at all levels," Roth added. \par \par \uc2  He reiterated that the SNB had no intention of setting a fixed parity for the franc against the euro because markets would not take it as an irrevocable decision. \par \par \uc2  "As long as Switzerland is not a member of the European Union, it will be difficult to convince the market that any parity of the Swiss franc will never be adjusted," he said. \par \par \uc2  "Any attempt to set a parity would thus stimulate speculation instead of calming it down. It is therefore in our interest to maintain a flexible relation between the Swiss franc and the euro." \par \par \uc2  A strong link between the franc and the euro could also endanger Switzerland's traditional advantage of having lower interest rates than elsewhere in Europe, he added. \par \par \uc2  Roth repeated that the SNB would not rule out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  or money markets to combat exchange rate fluctuations that it considered out of line with economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  "A relaxation of monetary policy in reaction to pressures on the Swiss franc is a clear option," he said, repeating the SNB's standard line. \par \par \uc2  He noted that the SNB had been able to keep the franc's fluctuations against the mark within acceptable margins over the past two years without trying to stabilise the exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  "Our intention is to maintain such a flexible approach when the Monetary Union starts on January 1, 1999," he said. \par \par \uc2  ((Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340 fax +41 1 202 5538, zurich.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926dubn03vcg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
