\par\par \b \uc2  Swiss Franc Maintains Upward Edge Vs DM, Rate Cut Talk \b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 1998\par 12:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  ZURICH (Dow Jones)--Upward pressure on the Swiss franc (CHF) against the Deutsche mark (DM) continues early afternoon Tuesday despite renewed money-market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Swiss National Bank. \par \par \uc2  For the third trading day running, the SNB Tuesday added generous liquidity to the money market, at a rate said by traders to be below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 1.0% discount rate. \par \par \uc2  The move led to brief mark gains to above CHF0.8050, but by 1120 GMT mark-franc cross trading was back to CHF0.8045. Late Tuesday, the mark was at CHF0.8034. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, dollar franc trading remains tightly range bound. One dollar currently buys CHF1.4618, down from CHF1.4643 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  'The SNB was in the money market again this morning,' said a trader at a bank in Liechtenstein. 'But (these liquidity injections) are only fighting the symptoms.' \par \par \uc2  Root cause of the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's unwelcome strength are its 'safe haven' image on the back of worries about European economic and monetary union, the stand-off in the Gulf and the Asian financial crisis. \par \par \uc2  In the interests of reviving the country's moribund economy, the SNB has fought since 1996 to bring the Swiss franc's strength down. The nearer the mark slips to CHF0.8000 the more speculation rises that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to cut its key discount rate. \par \par \uc2  'I expect we'll get to test CHF0.8000 again this week,' said another trader in \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Should this barrier be breached, direct \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or a discount rate cut could be on the cards, he said. \par \par \uc2  While the mark has strengthened against the franc in comparison to Monday, traders noted persistent selling of the German \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  above CHF0.8050. \par \par \uc2  Support is currently pegged at CHF0.8025-0.8030, with traders eying Friday's franc-high of CHF0.8012 as a vital marker beyond that. \par \par \uc2  Whether Thursday's meeting of the SNB directorate will bring a rate cut is far from certain. Some traders said the SNB may be happy to continue its money-market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  for some time yet before reaching for more drastic tools. \par \par \uc2  By Gerrit Wiesmann; 41-1-211-6637 \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 17-02-98 \par \par \uc2  1146GMT \par \par \uc2  1050 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du2h01asa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
