\par\par \b \uc2  Official  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves surge in 1995 - BIS. \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BASLE, \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 , June 10 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to brake and reverse the dollar's decline against the yen and mark in 1995 boosted official \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at the fastest pace since 1987, the Bank for International Settlements (BIS) said. \par \par \uc2  In its annual report, BIS also said the dollar's share in global official reserves had remained stable in the 1990s at about two-thirds, surprising many observers. \par \par \uc2  Dollar reserve growth in 1995 of $121 billion accounted for more than two-thirds of the growth in exchange-rate adjusted reserves of $168 billion. \par \par \uc2  The amounts of official \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves outstanding at end-1995 amounted to $1.36 trillion with dollar reserves amounting to $881 billion. \par \par \uc2  "The similarity to 1987 extends to the reliance of the United States on official sources of funds to finance the bulk of its $153 billion current account deficit," BIS said. \par \par \uc2  Net of the $6.0 billion build-up in reserves by U.S. authorities, financing by central banks and other official holders totalled about $115 billion. \par \par \uc2  "Thus, central banks and governments financed more than two-thirds of the U.S. current account deficit, much the same proportion as in 1987," BIS added. \par \par \uc2  BIS said the dollar's share in global official reserves had remained stable in the 1990s, surprising many observers in light of the long list of countries that are thought to have diversified their reserves away from the dollar. \par \par \uc2  But the apparent contradiction is resolved by looking at the country composition of reserve growth, BIS said. \par \par \uc2  "Developing countries with \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  closely aligned with the dollar, and with reserves weighted more towards the dollar that the global average, have been gaining reserves at a higher-than-average rate," BIS said. \par \par \uc2  BIS added that the willingness of investors to buy into the money and equity markets of developing countries suggests that these countries' reserves will continue to grow. \par \par \uc2  -- Peter Nielsen, Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011018ds6a06uoo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
