\par\par \b \uc2  Swiss central banker questions value of  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juni 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ZURICH, June 2 (Reuter) - The head of \b \highlight22\uc2 Switzerland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  challenged the value of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Friday, saying experience showed it was costly. \par \par \uc2  Swiss National Bank President Markus Lusser said his bank and most other central banks had grown "increasingly sceptical about the benefits of short-term exchange rate management." \par \par \uc2  His comments in a speech prepared for delivery in Los Angeles came just two days after his own bank joined the U.S. Federal Reserve and 10 other central banks to buy dollars in a coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that caught markets by surprise. \par \par \uc2  SNB officials have often said privately they doubt the value of trying to manipulate the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. They say the bank generally only takes part in coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to show solidarity with other central banks. \par \par \uc2  Lusser said the SNB had come under pressure again recently from trade unions, industrialists and people in the Swiss tourism sector to curb the Swiss franc's strength because of what they saw as its adverse impact on the economy. \par \par \uc2  But he noted the SNB's attempts in 1978 and 1987 to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt a soaring franc had been unhappy experiences. \par \par \uc2  Heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in late 1978 to try to keep the German mark above 80 Swiss centimes had caused the money supply to jump. After a delay, inflation rose sharply too and the economy did not get back to normal till 1983, he added. \par \par \uc2  Lusser said the situation in 1987 was similar. The franc had been appreciating for two years when the SNB loosened monetary policy to try to make the economy competitive again. The result was that "in 1989, with the usual time lag of two years, inflation began to rise sharply." \par \par \uc2  He went on: "With benefit of hindsight, we realise that even brief \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have turned out to be more costly than originally anticipated." \par \par \uc2  The long-term costs of inflation by far outweighed the benefits of a short-term depreciation, he added. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr62075d1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
